[center][font=Arial][size=6][color=#FCEE0A][b]CONFLICT STUDIO[/b][/color][/size][/font]
[color=#00F0FF]Profile-aware archive and code conflict management for Cyberpunk 2077[/color]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qcargile/Cyberpunk-Conflict-Studio/main/docs/nexus/media/00-overview.gif[/img]
[/center]
[line]

[font=Arial][size=5][color=#FCEE0A][b]▍ CREDIT FIRST[/b][/color][/size][/font]

[font=Arial]Conflict Studio exists because [b]rfuzzo[/b] built the original [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/11126]Archive Conflict Checker[/url]. Its archive browser, conflict dots, inline file groups, and load-order workflow were the starting point for this project. Please [b]endorse rfuzzo's original tool instead of this one[/b]. You can also view rfuzzo's [url=https://github.com/rfuzzo/Cyberpunk-utility]source code on GitHub[/url].[/font]

[font=Arial]Conflict Studio is a separate implementation with no copied code or assets from the original tool.[/font]
[line]

[font=Arial][size=5][color=#FCEE0A][b]▍ BETA[/b][/color][/size][/font]

[font=Arial][color=#FCEE0A][b]This is a beta.[/b][/color] Archive inspection, profile discovery, live previews, verified writes, backups, undo, and code checks have been tested. Some code interactions still require an in-game check. Export a support report when something looks wrong instead of treating every warning as a compatibility verdict.[/font]

[font=Arial][b]Quick antivirus note:[/b] Conflict Studio is an unsigned self-contained Windows application, so SmartScreen or antivirus software may warn about a new executable. The complete source is public at [url=https://github.com/qcargile/Cyberpunk-Conflict-Studio]GitHub[/url], and every release includes a SHA-256 checksum. Do not download it from mirrors.[/font]
[line]

[font=Arial][size=5][color=#FCEE0A][b]▍ OVERVIEW[/b][/color][/size][/font]

[font=Arial]Conflict Studio checks the active profile and shows which files, archives, methods, and values win. It understands MO2 priority, Vortex deployment, REDmods, modlist.txt, RedScript, CET Lua, TweakXL, and ArchiveXL.[/font]

[font=Arial]The goal is not to label every overlap as broken. It separates proven conflicts, file replacements, order-sensitive values, cases that need one runtime check, and overlaps that the framework can compose safely.[/font]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qcargile/Cyberpunk-Conflict-Studio/main/docs/nexus/media/01-overview.png[/img]
[line]

[font=Arial][size=5][color=#FCEE0A][b]▍ ARCHIVE CONFLICTS[/b][/color][/size][/font]
[list]
[*][font=Arial]Shows every active archive in actual load order.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Arial]Separates files an archive wins, loses, shares identically, or cannot determine.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Arial]Selecting an archive highlights only the archives it overrides and the archives that override it.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Arial]Drag one archive or a multi-selection. Edge scrolling accelerates with pointer depth, and the mouse wheel works during the drag.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Arial]The conflict pane updates before Apply, with an explicit unapplied state.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Arial]Apply creates a backup, verifies the write, rescans the profile, and supports Undo.[/font][/*]
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qcargile/Cyberpunk-Conflict-Studio/main/docs/nexus/media/02-archive-win.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qcargile/Cyberpunk-Conflict-Studio/main/docs/nexus/media/03-archive-loss.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qcargile/Cyberpunk-Conflict-Studio/main/docs/nexus/media/04-archive-expanded.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qcargile/Cyberpunk-Conflict-Studio/main/docs/nexus/media/07-unapplied-warning.png[/img]
[line]

[font=Arial][size=5][color=#FCEE0A][b]▍ CODE INTERACTIONS[/b][/color][/size][/font]

[font=Arial]Conflict Studio also inspects active RedScript, CET Lua, TweakXL, ArchiveXL, and loose-file ownership. Proven exclusive replacements are separated from values where the last assignment wins, file overrides, compatible composition, and cases that need one specific runtime check.[/font]

[font=Arial]Each row explains what happens, which mods are involved, why it matters, and what to do next. Saved reviews reset when the relevant files or profile change.[/font]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qcargile/Cyberpunk-Conflict-Studio/main/docs/nexus/media/05-code-overview.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qcargile/Cyberpunk-Conflict-Studio/main/docs/nexus/media/06-code-conflict.png[/img]
[line]

[font=Arial][size=5][color=#FCEE0A][b]▍ REQUIREMENTS[/b][/color][/size][/font]

[list]
[*][font=Arial]Windows 10 version 2004 or newer, 64-bit.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Arial]A Cyberpunk 2077 installation or an active MO2/Vortex profile.[/font][/*]
[/list]

[font=Arial]No Cyberpunk framework dependency and no separate .NET installation are required. The runtime is bundled into ConflictStudio.exe.[/font]
[line]

[font=Arial][size=5][color=#FCEE0A][b]▍ MO2 SETUP[/b][/color][/size][/font]

[spoiler=Show MO2 setup]
[list=1]
[*][font=Arial]Download the ZIP manually. [b]Do not install it as an MO2 mod.[/b][/font][/*]
[*][font=Arial]Extract it anywhere outside the MO2 instance's mods folder. [b]<MO2 instance>\tools\Conflict Studio[/b] works.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Arial]Add [b]Conflict Studio\ConflictStudio.exe[/b] to MO2's executable list.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Arial]Set Start in to the MO2 instance folder containing ModOrganizer.ini.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Arial]Use arguments: [b]--manager mo2 --profile current[/b].[/font][/*]
[*][font=Arial]Under Settings → Workarounds → Executables Blacklist, add [b]ConflictStudio.exe[/b], restart MO2, and choose Continue when MO2 warns that the tool is blacklisted.[/font][/*]
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qcargile/Cyberpunk-Conflict-Studio/main/docs/nexus/media/08-mo2-tool-setup.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qcargile/Cyberpunk-Conflict-Studio/main/docs/nexus/media/09-mo2-settings-navigation.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qcargile/Cyberpunk-Conflict-Studio/main/docs/nexus/media/10-mo2-blacklist.png[/img]
[/spoiler]
[line]

[font=Arial][size=5][color=#FCEE0A][b]▍ VORTEX SETUP[/b][/color][/size][/font]

[spoiler=Show Vortex setup]
[list=1]
[*][font=Arial]Download the same ZIP manually.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Arial]Open Extensions in Vortex's advanced mode and drop the ZIP onto the extension installer.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Arial]Restart Vortex, activate the Cyberpunk profile, and deploy it.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Arial]Open Cyberpunk 2077 → Tools and launch Conflict Studio.[/font][/*]
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qcargile/Cyberpunk-Conflict-Studio/main/docs/nexus/media/11-vortex-extensions-navigation.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qcargile/Cyberpunk-Conflict-Studio/main/docs/nexus/media/12-vortex-extension-enabled.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qcargile/Cyberpunk-Conflict-Studio/main/docs/nexus/media/13-vortex-tool-launch.png[/img]
[/spoiler]
[line]

[font=Arial][size=5][color=#FCEE0A][b]▍ IMPORTANT[/b][/color][/size][/font]
[list]
[*][font=Arial]Do not scan the same game installation as MO2 while Vortex files remain deployed. Conflict Studio blocks mixed-manager scans.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Arial]Cyberpunk must be closed before archive-order writes. MO2 or Vortex may remain open.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Arial]Conflict Studio does not merge archives or automatically write compatibility patches.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Arial]Static overlap is not automatically a gameplay conflict.[/font][/*]
[/list]

[font=Arial][b]Large profiles:[/b] The first scan can take several minutes because Conflict Studio fingerprints archive contents. Later scans reuse cached fingerprints when the files are unchanged. Conflict Studio is intentionally excluded from MO2's VFS so it can read the physical provider folders and identify the winning mod.[/font]

[font=Arial][b]MO2 paths:[/b] The MO2 program, instance, profiles, mods, and overwrite folders may be on different drives. Start in must point to the instance folder containing ModOrganizer.ini. A missing configured mods directory now produces a direct setup error.[/font]

[font=Arial][b]Incomplete archive order:[/b] Conflict Studio prepares a complete repair draft. It preserves the valid listed order, removes duplicate or inactive entries, adds missing active archives, and previews the result before Apply.[/font]

[font=Arial]When reporting a problem, reproduce it once and use the Support tab to copy or save the privacy-filtered report.[/font]
[line]

